  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently as of typing the \"limits\" on Quest are 10,000 Polygons, 2 Skinned Meshes, 2 Meshes, 4 Materials, 200 Particles, \n(Note Bounds Size is not listed bound size has no effect on anything)\nWe have done a lot of tests to see the quests real limits, so far we found that it can handle 500,000 polygons just fine with 20 users in the same model thus total of 10 million  but VR 2x the polygons due to rendering it per eye so 20 million polygons was being rendered per quest user and only 3-4 fps was lost and 6-8 fps was lost with a mirror reflecting all 20 making 40 million, so really the Quest can handle the same polygons that the pc can handle so it should be the exact limit the current pc polygon limit is set to. we also tested the materials they are able to handle 100 materials on an avatar with 3-9 fps lost so really the current limit is way lower then what the quest can handle, the new limit should be the same as the PC limit is for quest can handle way more then what is currently set.",
